# The upstream commit this fork has been reviewed against.
#
# The fork's git history is squashed and disjoint from upstream's, so comparing
# by commit reports all ~730 upstream commits as "missing" - including "First
# commit" - which is useless. The upstream-watch workflow therefore reports only
# commits AFTER the SHA below, and this SHA is advanced as each batch is triaged.
#
# Triaged 2026-08-12, content-first (reading our functions, not matching commit
# hashes), covering the 22 commits from 4fb63e806758 to 5ce853685dec:
#
#   - 19 ALREADY PRESENT, several as supersets of upstream's fix. Our partial-FETCH
#     clamp additionally handles negative start and negative count, which upstream
#     still does not.
#   - bc9e37750abe (TLSOptions #520) SUPERSEDED: the two UI files it changes do not
#     exist here (the classic Administrator and the PHP WebAdmin were replaced),
#     and we enforce the ChaCha constraint server-side in SslContextInitializer,
#     which upstream does not do at all.
#   - 5ce853685dec (libpq 15.18) NOT APPLICABLE: a downgrade. We are deliberately
#     ahead on the dependency set (PostgreSQL 18.3, OpenSSL 4.0.x, Boost 1.91).
#   - Nothing required porting.
#
# Two upstream hunks are deliberately NOT taken and should stay that way:
#   - From 61c6e3cb3b7f (#528): "if (error == boost::asio::error::eof) return;"
#     inside the read-error branch. It returns before popping the read operation
#     and before EnqueueDisconnect, leaking the operation and leaving the session
#     open, and it suppresses OnReadError - which is what marks recipients when a
#     remote server hangs up mid-delivery. We handle the same case by disconnecting
#     after an end-of-stream instead.
#   - The libpq downgrade above.
#
# Known cosmetic-only divergence from 02b7f1e00278 (#530), tracked but not taken:
# the Delimeter->Delimiter and has_on_too_many_invalid_comands_ renames, a
# #define -> constexpr, and some comment typos. Semantically identical; taking
# them would only reduce future textual merge friction.
#
# Update this SHA (and only this SHA) when a batch has been triaged.
